BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:First Christian Church
DTSTART:20151101T210000Z
DTEND:20151101T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260808T022315Z
UID:tgkg1cuoals30pbjqev9rtf1dc@google.com
CREATED:20151001T155604Z
DESCRIPTION:The choirs of First Christian Church Bloomington and First Pres
 byterian Church with special guest artist mezzo-soprano Mary Ann Hart will 
 present a benefit concert for the Interfaith Winter Shelter.\n\nThe First C
 hristian Church (Disciples of Christ) Bloomington Sanctuary Choir will once
  again join with the Chancel Choir of First Presbyterian Church to present 
 a benefit concert for the Interfaith Winter Shelter (IFWS)\, a low-barrier 
 winter homeless shelter that offers overnight lodging to men and women from
  November 1 to March 31. The free concert will take place November 1\, 2015
 \, at 4 p.m. at FCC Bloomington\, 205 E. Kirkwood Avenue\, Bloomington\, In
 diana 47408. A freewill offering will be taken to support the work of the s
 helter.\n\nBluegrass music and contemporary choral composition lovers will 
 especially enjoy this year’s major piece\, which combines a setting of the 
 traditional Mass texts alternating with a beautiful poem by Marcia Chamberl
 ain about the environment\, the human condition\, and humanity’s place in t
 he world. The piece\, Carol Barnett’s The World Beloved: A Bluegrass Mass\,
  was composed for the VocalEssence chorus and Monroe Crossing Bluegrass ban
 d and combines the styles of bluegrass music with contemporary choral compo
 sition.\n\nThe concert will be led by renowned conductors Dr. Jan Harringto
 n\, chancellor's professor of conducting emeritus\, Indiana University Jaco
 bs School of Music and director of First Christian Church’s choir\, and Dr.
  Katy Strand\, associate professor of music (Music Education) and chair of 
 Music Education\, Indiana University Jacobs School of Music and director of
  First Presbyterian Church’s choir. Special guest Mary Ann Hart is chair of
  the Voice Department at Indiana University Jacobs School of Music. Hart ha
 s won numerous song competitions\, including the Carnegie Hall Internationa
 l American Music Competition\, Concert Artists Guild\, and National Associa
 tion of Teachers of Singing (NATS) Artist awards\; she also received a gran
 t from the National Endowment for the Arts.\n\nFor more about the IFWS\, vi
 sit http://interfaithwintershelter.org.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260411T190449Z
LOCATION:First Christian Church\, 205 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 474
 08\, United States
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Bluegrass Mass Concert for IFWS
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
